{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081123-armor-and-penalties","id":1081123,"title":"Armor and penalties","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-19T15:30:55-07:00","id":1081123,"title":"Armor and penalties","content":"What are you interpretation on armor penalty rules<br /> <br /> On one hand the dex penalty is on all Dexterity based actions except for those realted to combat.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it for all dex based actions. Period.<br /> <br /> I've seen and used both and i'm curious what you think. Arguments could be made for both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:09:43-07:00","id":1081144,"title":"","content":"All Dexterity-based rolls, including combat. I generally house rule it though that you suffer armor penalties equal to (Armor Soak - (Strength + Potence)), so strong characters suffer less penalties than weak characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:13:14-07:00","id":1081147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081123-armor-and-penalties?p=1081144#post1081144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Dexterity-based rolls, including combat. I generally house rule it though that you suffer armor penalties equal to (Armor Soak - (Strength + Potence)), so strong characters suffer less penalties than weak characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if that Armor is made by Lore of Forge? (Demon Lore) The Lore of forge can actually lower the penalty and Increase the Soaking Dices upto the double.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12843-mkjmn","name":"Mkjmn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:20:20-07:00","id":1081152,"title":"","content":"I too am a fan of all dex based rolls, I call it the &quot;Randy Parker&quot; rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:24:21-07:00","id":1081154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mkjmn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1081123-armor-and-penalties?p=1081147#post1081147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if that Armor is made by Lore of Forge? (Demon Lore) The Lore of forge can actually lower the penalty and Increase the Soaking Dices upto the double.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is magic, so calculate required Strength by the base soak and reduce the armor penalty for weaker characters (no particular bonus for strong characters). The same could apply to armor of exceptional quality (if you use such rules in your games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T16:36:20-07:00","id":1081162,"title":"","content":"What about penalty applies to all rolls including combat. However, people with sufficient training (Ranged/Melee/Etc at 2+) negate 1 penalty dice for each dot they have in the used trait. So for example a character with Firearms 2 and Melee 1, who is used to fighting in heavy armor (Dex penalty 3) can negate 2 of the penalty (for a total of 1 penalty) when shooting but would have the full penalty when fighting with a knife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T08:07:14-07:00","id":1085036,"title":"","content":"It's quite well stated through out the years that the Dexterity penalty <b><i>doesn't </i></b>apply to combat actions, as that'd be utterly pointless. Logic and common sense need only be applied to figure out how shooting a gun or swinging a sword is unaffected by the penalty. How would a knight or soldier do their job if their armor made swinging nigh impossible. The specifics of the rule say <i><b>most</b></i> Dexterity rolls.<br /> <br /> The rule was meant for movement based actions, like sprinting and running and I guess parkour if you really wanted to do that in plate armor. There was a rule in Dark Ages Revised where if you had Melee 3, the penalty was halved. Personally I just make it Athletics 3 and called it a day. Armor is quite terrible for the most part and throwing in more penalties makes it worse.<br /> <br /> Also have the thread from a few months back.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/918148-v20-armor-rules\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/918148-v20-armor-rules\"> V20 Armor Rules - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/918148-v20-armor-rules\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/918148-v20-armor-rules </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Could someone with experience wearing armour speak to the armour rules in V20? From VtM 20th AE, p. 280: The penalties listed seem excessive, to put it mildly. I've interacted with police officers wearing full riot gear and while they'd be incapable of doing cartwheels, I can assure you that their Dexterity+Brawl pools weren't significantly affected by their armour. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":2414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","user":"theoutlander523","date":". 04-28-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}